## Context

Child of [[0870]]. The integration review of the served views (7aae8a9d
against 881b1262) found that the retirement of the legacy readers
([[0878]]) left `scripts/jetp/_country_views_v2.py` hard-coding
`funders=[]`, `claims=[]` and `source_links=[]` for every project (entered
at dc9a0645): totals before and after, source_links 315 to 0, claims 136
to 0, project funders 84 to 0. The ledger holds 0 `refers_to` rows and 0
discovery line-referents; the 304 legacy links sit in
`data/jetp/migration/0874-link-candidates.csv`.

Author decisions (2026-09-29):

- Option D: the legacy links are not promoted now; M2 (tracker [[1500]])
  resolves them into candidate rows after blind extraction.
- A field is filled only from ledger rows (derived, never typed). A field
  the ledger cannot support, or whose content is already served under
  another name, is removed from the served contract together with the
  reading code in `deliverables/jetp-observatory/app.js`.
- A coverage row (`config/jetp-ledger.sql`, `coverage`) is a review
  record: it says what was collected for a referent, not what a document
  says. Its `document_ids` are shown on the project page in a block of
  their own, labelled as collected in the coverage review of
  `checked_at` and not cited, never merged into the cited documents and
  never counted as support.
- Recipe VN3 of [[0834]] (Bac Ai shows six sources) is amended to what
  the ledger supports: one cited document and six collected in the
  coverage block. VN3 stays a manual recipe step; no new automated guard
  without a skeptical advisor first.
- Each document shows the state of our collection and reading, derived at
  build time from the ledger and stored nowhere: not collected (no
  snapshot), collected but not extracted (a snapshot, no line), stub (the
  one minimal line the migration minted to hold a locator,
  `docs/jetp-ledger-migration.md` step 3), extracted (lines an extractor
  read). "Fully ingested" and the terminal grey states come with M2 and
  are not shown yet. Each state has a word and an icon, not colour alone,
  reads in grayscale, and the legend is labelled "State of our collection
  and reading".
- `check_facts` in `tests/browser/jetp_observatory.py` is dead code
  (never called by `check_site`, stale Bac Ai identifier, typed constant
  3) and is deleted.
- The navigation is not restructured here (a later ticket does that).

## Relevant files

- `scripts/jetp/_country_views_v2.py`: the country views
- `scripts/jetp/build_ledger_documents_view.py`: the documents view the
  Documents page joins on the identifier, which carries the state
- `deliverables/jetp-observatory/app.js`, `styles.css`
- `tests/test_jetp_country_views_v2.py`, `tests/test_jetp_ledger_documents_view.py`,
  `tests/test_jetp_observatory_render.py`, `tests/browser/jetp_observatory.py`
- `docs/jetp-study/0834-integration-review-final-2026-09-22.md`: recipe VN3

## Exit criteria

- [ ] For each of `funders`, `claims`, `source_links`: either filled from
      ledger rows (which rows, how many) or removed from the served
      contract and from app.js, with the reason recorded in the PR
- [ ] The project page shows a block "Collected in the coverage review of
      <checked_at> (not cited)" listing the coverage row's `document_ids`
      with links, separate from the cited documents and counted nowhere
- [ ] `check_facts` is deleted; the VN3 recipe text reads: Bac Ai shows
      one cited document and six collected in the coverage block
- [ ] Every document carries a collection state (not collected, collected
      but not extracted, stub, extracted), derived at build time, shown
      with a word and an icon on the Documents page and wherever a
      document is listed, under the legend "State of our collection and
      reading"; the stub rule is stated and its count reported
- [ ] Page copy uses no banned word (claims, deals, players, sources,
      entities, records) in the text this ticket adds
- [ ] Tests first for the builder changes; every served file byte-diffed
      before and after, each change listed with counts; the build is
      byte-identical when run twice and on padme; `make lint`,
      `make check-fast`, `make check-jetp` on padme;
      `tests/browser/jetp_observatory.py` passes against the built site
